---
/**
 * About (playbook 4.3): the guide, not the hero. Empathy headline → why this
 * exists (the 9-in-10 finding) → authority → values → CTA. E-E-A-T page.
 */
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Breadcrumbs from '../components/Breadcrumbs.astro';
import ImageSlot from '../components/ImageSlot.astro';
import CtaBand from '../components/CtaBand.astro';
import { SITE, CTA } from '../config';
import { person } from '../lib/schema';

const crumbs = [
  { name: 'Home', path: '/' },
  { name: 'About', path: '/about' },
];
---

<Layout
  title="About — Why This Service Exists | Marketing Executive VA"
  description="I spent a year speaking with thousands of UK business owners about their marketing. Nine in ten were doing little or none — not from neglect, but because nobody owned it. This service is the answer."
  path="/about"
  schema={[person()]}
>
  <section class="section">
    <div class="wrap about-grid">
      <div class="about-side">
        <ImageSlot label="Founder headshot, warm natural light, 4:5" />
        <div class="side-facts card">
          <h2>The short version</h2>
          <ul>
            <li>One operator, your whole marketing function</li>
            <li>A year qualifying SMBs for eBay’s Start&nbsp;Up–Scale&nbsp;Up programme</li>
            <li>Tens of thousands of calls; thousands of owner conversations</li>
            <li>Based in the {SITE.country}, working remotely with businesses anywhere</li>
            <!-- [TODO-HUMAN] add: real name, years in marketing, credentials/certs, notable employers -->
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="about-main">
        <Breadcrumbs crumbs={crumbs} />
        <p class="eyebrow">About</p>
        <h1>You know marketing matters. You’ve just never had anyone own it.</h1>
        <p class="about-open">
          I know that’s true of most small businesses — because I heard it, first-hand, thousands of times.
        </p>
        <p>
          From January 2025 to January 2026 I worked on eBay’s Start Up–Scale Up programme,
          qualifying small and mid-size businesses for support. The job was volume: 200 to 500
          dials a day, every working day, for a year — tens of thousands of calls, and real
          conversations with thousands of business owners about how they find customers.
        </p>
        <p>
          One pattern repeated until it was impossible to ignore: <strong>roughly nine out of ten
          of those businesses were doing little or no marketing — or doing it half-heartedly.</strong>
          A site nobody had touched in years. A Facebook page that stopped in 2023. A freelancer
          who'd moved on. And almost every owner said a version of the same sentence:
          <em>“I know we should be doing more, I just don’t have the time.”</em>
        </p>
        <p>
          These weren’t bad businesses. Many were excellent — busy precisely because they were
          good. That’s the unfairness of it: the better you are at the work, the less time you have
          to tell anyone, and the more ground you quietly give to competitors who are louder but
          not better.
        </p>

        <h2>Why “one person” is the answer, not the compromise</h2>
        <p>
          The standard advice to those owners is “hire an agency” or “hire a marketer.” But a
          £2,000+ monthly retainer or a £40,000 salary isn’t realistic at this size — and the
          scatter of freelancers most owners try instead just hands them a coordination job they
          didn’t want. What a 1–25-person business actually needs is simpler:
          <strong>one experienced person who owns the whole function</strong> — the plan, the
          execution, and the honest report on whether it worked.
        </p>
        <p>
          That’s the entire model here. I run your marketing as a monthly subscription:
          strategy, website, search, ads, email, content, reporting — end to end, in your name,
          with <a href="/how-it-works">unlimited revisions and no long contract</a>. You stay in
          the loop, not in the weeds.
        </p>

        <h2>How I work</h2>
        <ul class="values">
          <li><strong>Honesty over theatre.</strong> The monthly report includes what didn’t work. Channels that don’t earn their place get cut, even when cutting them shrinks my to-do list.</li>
          <li><strong>Your name on everything.</strong> Accounts, content, data — all owned by you from day one. Leaving should be clean enough that you never feel held hostage.</li>
          <li><strong>Plain English.</strong> If a report needs a glossary, it’s a bad report.</li>
          <li><strong>Proof before claims.</strong> This site has empty case-study slots rather than invented numbers. They’ll fill with real, named results — slowly, and honestly.</li>
        </ul>

        <p class="about-cta-line">
          If any of this sounds like your business, the next step is a
          {SITE.booking.callLength} conversation — {SITE.booking.promise.toLowerCase()}
        </p>
        <a href={SITE.booking.url} class="btn" data-event="cta_click" data-event-loc="about_body">{CTA.direct}</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <CtaBand heading="Marketing owned, moving, and reported on." loc="about_final" />
</Layout>

<style>
  .about-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 0.72fr 1.28fr;
    gap: clamp(32px, 5vw, 64px);
    align-items: start;
  }

  .about-side {
    position: sticky;
    top: 90px;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 20px;
  }

  .side-facts h2 {
    font-family: var(--font-body);
    font-size: 0.8rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.14em;
    color: var(--stone);
    margin-bottom: 12px;
  }

  .side-facts ul {
    list-style: none;
    margin: 0;
    padding: 0;
  }

  .side-facts li {
    padding: 8px 0;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--tint);
    font-size: 0.9rem;
  }

  .about-main h1 {
    margin-top: 24px;
  }

  .about-open {
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-style: italic;
    font-size: 1.3rem;
    line-height: 1.4;
    margin-block: 20px 24px;
  }

  .about-main h2 {
    margin-top: 40px;
  }

  .values {
    list-style: none;
    padding: 0;
    margin: 20px 0;
  }

  .values li {
    padding: 12px 0;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--tint);
  }

  .about-cta-line {
    margin-top: 32px;
    font-weight: 500;
  }

  @media (max-width: 880px) {
    .about-grid {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }

    .about-side {
      position: static;
      max-width: 420px;
    }
  }
</style>
